3. Modifications by Hanzo
================================================================================

    Copyright 2026 Hanzo AI, Inc.

Hanzo's modifications begin 2026-03-01. They are licensed under AGPL-3.0, on
the same terms as the upstream work. In summary, Hanzo has:

  * Replaced authentication with Hanzo IAM (hanzo.id) as a dedicated
    OIDC/OAuth identity provider.
  * Moved persistence from PostgreSQL to Hanzo Base (SQLite), using a single
    shared database file with team-scoped tenancy.
  * Replaced PostHog product analytics with Hanzo Insights.
  * Removed the commercial billing surface. This distribution has no paywalls
    and no plan tiers; every team receives the full feature set under AGPL.
  * Rebranded from Documenso to Hanzo Sign — names, metadata, page titles,
    Open Graph tags, email templates, legal references and social handles —
    and added white-label hooks so the brand resolves per deployment.
  * Restyled the user interface (dark, monochrome, centered IAM sign-in).
  * Renamed the npm packages from the @documenso/* scope to @hanzo/esign-*.
  * Upgraded the toolchain to TypeScript 5.9 and React Router 7.13, and
    migrated the workspace to pnpm.
  * Replaced the CI/CD pipeline with the native Hanzo pipeline
    (git.hanzo.ai + cd.hanzo.ai) and containerised the app for Kubernetes.


